  "faq": {
    "eyebrow": "Frequently asked questions",
    "title": "We answer your most common questions",
    "lead": "Find clear answers about preparation, turnaround times, and practical aspects of your lab tests. If you still have questions, you can always contact us in the contact section.",
    "items": [
      {
        "question": "Can I get tests done without an appointment?",
        "answer": "Yes, we accept walk-ins during business hours. However, scheduling in advance helps reduce waiting times."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do you attend children and older adults?",
        "answer": "Yes, we have trained staff for sample collection in patients of all ages."
      },
      {
        "question": "What documents should I bring?",
        "answer": "Usually you only need an ID and a medical order if your test requires it."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do I need to fast before a test?",
        "answer": "It depends on the type of analysis. Some tests, such as glucose or lipid profile, require 8 to 12 hours of fasting. We recommend checking specific instructions in advance."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is a medical order required?",
        "answer": "Some tests require medical indication, while others can be done by direct patient request."
      },
      {
        "question": "How should I prepare for my test?",
        "answer": "Instructions vary by study. Our team will provide the required recommendations when scheduling your appointment."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I take several tests on the same day?",
        "answer": "Yes, in most cases multiple tests can be done in a single visit, as long as preparation instructions are met."
      },
      {
        "question": "How long does it take to get results?",
        "answer": "Most tests are delivered the same day or within 24 hours. Some specialized studies may require more time."
      },
      {
        "question": "How can I receive my results?",
        "answer": "You can receive them at our facilities or, if available, via digital delivery to your registered email."
      },
      {
        "question": "Is my result information confidential?",
        "answer": "Yes, we guarantee protection and confidentiality of all data and results according to security and professional ethics standards."
      },
      {
        "question": "How often should I get routine tests?",
        "answer": "A general check-up is recommended at least once a year. However, frequency may vary according to age, medical history, and your doctor's recommendations."
      },
      {
        "question": "How important is it to get tests even if I feel fine?",
        "answer": "Many conditions may develop without visible symptoms. Clinical tests help detect changes early and prevent future complications."
      },
      {
        "question": "At what age should I start preventive check-ups?",
        "answer": "Check-ups can start in adolescence, but from age 30 onward closer preventive follow-up is recommended, especially with family history."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which tests are part of a basic check-up?",
        "answer": "They usually include complete blood count, glucose, lipid profile, and general urine test. The doctor may request additional studies based on each case."
      }
    ]
  },
